1
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:31,039
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

2
00:03:31,039 --> 00:03:37,039
世界波に乗ろう 力合わせて

3
00:03:37,039 --> 00:03:45,039
ときめく方へ急ごう 始まりの合図

4
00:03:45,039 --> 00:03:52,039
今こそ船出の時 光を上げたら

5
00:03:52,039 --> 00:04:00,039
七色の風を切り 冒険の海へ

6
00:04:00,039 --> 00:04:07,039
傷だらけの旅だけど 大事なものがそこにある

7
00:04:07,039 --> 00:04:14,039
臨時ならいつだって 僕が守るから

8
00:04:14,039 --> 00:04:18,039
大丈夫さ 前に進もう

9
00:04:18,039 --> 00:04:22,039
太陽をいつも胸に

10
00:04:22,039 --> 00:04:25,039
嵐が来たら肩組んで

11
00:04:25,039 --> 00:04:29,039
その滝の光を見よう

12
00:04:29,039 --> 00:04:33,039
夢の欠片集まれば

13
00:04:33,039 --> 00:04:36,039
明日に向かう地図になる

14
00:04:36,039 --> 00:04:43,039
だから同じ旗のもと 願いをつかわえようよ

15
00:04:43,039 --> 00:04:47,039
僕らはひとつわき

16
00:04:47,039 --> 00:04:56,959
S.T.R.P. 日本に recursがおっしゃない

17
00:04:57,039 --> 00:05:05,099
新しい Sport

18
00:05:05,099 --> 00:05:10,099
Well, I'm not mistaken, am I?

19
00:05:10,099 --> 00:05:11,999
Gates of Justice

20
00:05:11,999 --> 00:05:13,279
新宿りました

21
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:20,739
judicial island. But that's a lie. The court they have there is only for show. The truth is, if you've

22
00:05:20,739 --> 00:05:26,299
been taken there, then you're already considered guilty. When you arrive, the government walks you

23
00:05:26,299 --> 00:05:32,099
through an empty courtroom, leading to a pair of cold steel doors that tower above the entire island.

24
00:05:34,659 --> 00:05:39,919
Those doors are known as the gates of justice. The criminals who walk through them must abandon

25
00:05:39,919 --> 00:05:45,799
all hope. Once they reach the other side, they'll never see the light of day again. Once you set sail

26
00:05:45,799 --> 00:05:51,019
beyond those doors, there are only two destinations you can reach, neither of which you are ever likely

27
00:05:51,019 --> 00:05:57,759
to leave. One is Navy Headquarters, where the strongest military powers in the world gather

28
00:05:57,759 --> 00:06:05,099
in the name of justice. The other is Impel Down, an underwater prison filled with torture chambers

29
00:06:05,099 --> 00:06:10,859
and execution blocks. No matter how vicious they may be, the criminals imprisoned there can only

30
00:06:10,859 --> 00:06:17,259
wait for death. In other words, going to Innie's lobby is no different than a death sentence.

31
00:06:18,019 --> 00:06:22,659
There's no trial, no justice, and no hope of escape. Am I right?

32
00:06:25,979 --> 00:06:31,299
Robin has a bounty on her head. No matter where they take her, she'll face death or worse.

33
00:06:31,299 --> 00:06:35,559
Every second we sit here talking, she gets one step closer to the gates of justice.

34
00:06:36,019 --> 00:06:38,539
Don't you dare tell us to wait until tomorrow!

35
00:06:45,759 --> 00:06:49,419
If you know that much already, I've only got one thing to say.

36
00:06:50,039 --> 00:06:55,799
Even if the sea was calm and you were able to set sail, that's the last place you should ever go.

37
00:06:56,139 --> 00:06:59,859
Don't forget, you people are wanted criminals just the same as your friend.

38
00:07:01,299 --> 00:07:06,539
Just like you said, Innie's lobby is the front door to the world government's own personal playground.

39
00:07:06,939 --> 00:07:10,459
They've drawn battle lines around that place that should never, ever be crossed.

40
00:07:11,299 --> 00:07:17,279
Regardless of how they feel about their crewmates, no pirate would be stupid enough to launch a rescue mission there.

41
00:07:17,599 --> 00:07:18,819
They know what would happen.

42
00:07:20,019 --> 00:07:23,839
Picking a fight in that place is like declaring war on the entire Navy!

43
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:31,339
Hey, I know how you must feel, but Pauly's right!

44
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:33,559
You can't leave during Aqua Laguna anyway!

45
00:07:33,779 --> 00:07:35,379
You'll be dead before you even get there!

46
00:07:35,439 --> 00:07:37,759
There's no point in throwing your lives away over this!

47
00:07:38,559 --> 00:07:38,959
Luffy?

48
00:07:41,479 --> 00:07:42,319
Find them!

49
00:07:43,059 --> 00:07:44,559
We'll steal the ship!

50
00:07:44,559 --> 00:07:54,379
Don't try to get in our way!

51
00:07:54,379 --> 00:07:56,339
We're leaving now!

52
00:07:56,339 --> 00:07:57,339
Whoa!

53
00:07:57,339 --> 00:08:03,759
Even the waves got bad!

54
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:05,619
Whoa!

55
00:08:05,619 --> 00:08:08,939
Is he gonna fight us?

56
00:08:08,939 --> 00:08:10,219
That sure was scary!

57
00:08:12,019 --> 00:08:12,659
Fine, then.

58
00:08:12,939 --> 00:08:14,699
You wanna fight, you got it!

59
00:08:22,139 --> 00:08:22,999
All of you!

60
00:08:23,459 --> 00:08:24,279
Stop it!

61
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:27,559
Kokoro?

62
00:08:28,399 --> 00:08:31,139
Stop being such a damn fool, Straw Hat!

63
00:08:31,139 --> 00:08:34,999
Like it or not, Pauly's right on this one.

64
00:08:35,359 --> 00:08:36,439
Shut up, Granny!

65
00:08:36,539 --> 00:08:37,579
It's none of your business!

66
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:39,779
You sure about that, boy?

67
00:08:40,459 --> 00:08:44,699
Either way, spokes are just trying to stop you from killing yourself.

68
00:08:45,339 --> 00:08:50,379
The point is, no matter how mad you are, no ship can handle Aqua Laguna.

69
00:08:50,959 --> 00:08:55,019
Only a sea train made by a legendary man stands a chance.

70
00:08:55,019 --> 00:09:00,539
I know that, but I don't have any choice, since the only sea train in the world has left town already!

71
00:09:00,539 --> 00:09:09,779
If you're prepared to die, then that's fine, just come along with me, we'll brave the storm on my sea train!

72
00:09:30,539 --> 00:09:37,699
Who's that guy?

73
00:09:37,779 --> 00:09:38,239
I don't know.

74
00:09:39,439 --> 00:09:40,319
You idiots!

75
00:09:40,619 --> 00:09:41,739
Don't just stand there!

76
00:09:41,839 --> 00:09:44,299
If he's not wearing a uniform, then he must be an intruder!

77
00:09:49,719 --> 00:09:50,599
Get him!

78
00:09:51,259 --> 00:09:53,899
I guess playing innocent doesn't work in here.

79
00:09:53,899 --> 00:10:06,739
And here I thought I could get out of a fight.

80
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:09,179
Oh well, it's not my funeral.

81
00:10:13,179 --> 00:10:13,739
Sanji?

82
00:10:14,439 --> 00:10:15,139
Hold it!

83
00:10:15,139 --> 00:10:21,579
You think we're going to let you get away with that?

84
00:10:22,459 --> 00:10:23,839
If you're smart.

85
00:10:26,139 --> 00:10:26,699
Ah!

86
00:10:30,699 --> 00:10:31,139
Okay!

87
00:10:34,939 --> 00:10:35,419
Rats!

88
00:10:35,419 --> 00:10:46,419
Wait, you didn't hijack the sea train just to rescue me, did you?

89
00:10:46,939 --> 00:10:49,259
I don't even know what you're doing here.

90
00:10:55,879 --> 00:10:57,359
Also, what's your name again?

91
00:10:57,459 --> 00:10:59,659
I don't believe we've actually met before, have we?

92
00:10:59,999 --> 00:11:02,239
Are you kidding me, you jerk?

93
00:11:02,239 --> 00:11:05,959
Bingo!

94
00:11:06,519 --> 00:11:07,479
Transponder snails!

95
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:11,799
Okay, this must be a communications room or something.

96
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:14,259
Lucky I ran into this place so soon.

97
00:11:15,179 --> 00:11:20,179
Those guys I beat up in the last card only had a bunch of useless crap masks and costumes and stuff.

98
00:11:20,559 --> 00:11:23,139
Anyway, now that I have this, I can get in touch with Nami!

99
00:11:23,799 --> 00:11:27,099
Let me guess, he's one of your pirate friends, isn't he?

100
00:11:27,299 --> 00:11:27,939
Ex-friend.

101
00:11:28,359 --> 00:11:29,939
The question is, who are you?

102
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:32,499
I'm the face of Water 7's underworld.

103
00:11:33,039 --> 00:11:34,719
The ship dismantler, Frankie.

104
00:11:34,719 --> 00:11:39,499
So you're the bastard who beat up Usopp, huh?

105
00:11:39,739 --> 00:11:42,959
He may be dead to me now, but he was part of our crew back then.

106
00:11:43,139 --> 00:11:45,219
How many pieces do you want me to cut you into?

107
00:11:45,659 --> 00:11:47,119
No, no, no, no, wait, wait, wait.

108
00:11:47,359 --> 00:11:48,599
It's not like that now.

109
00:11:48,719 --> 00:11:50,319
A lot of stuff's changed since then.

110
00:11:50,579 --> 00:11:51,619
Hey, punk!

111
00:11:51,819 --> 00:11:53,559
You're lucky I'm tied up!

112
00:11:53,779 --> 00:11:54,559
Come on, man.

113
00:11:54,599 --> 00:11:55,759
That line's getting old.

114
00:11:56,339 --> 00:11:57,719
Seriously, he's a good guy.

115
00:11:57,719 --> 00:12:00,279
He saved the Mary, at least for a while.

116
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,019
Oh, yeah.

117
00:12:04,439 --> 00:12:05,719
The Mary was...

118
00:12:06,239 --> 00:12:07,719
Whoa!

119
00:12:08,479 --> 00:12:09,379
Come on, buddy.

120
00:12:09,439 --> 00:12:11,419
You can't get all sad and mopey on me now.

121
00:12:11,799 --> 00:12:13,539
Hey, Blondie, untie me!

122
00:12:13,759 --> 00:12:14,659
Pretty please!

123
00:12:14,659 --> 00:12:19,299
You can spend the rest of your life in that potato sack for all I care.

124
00:12:19,679 --> 00:12:20,619
Screw you!

125
00:12:21,079 --> 00:12:22,219
I said pretty please.

126
00:12:22,279 --> 00:12:23,499
What the hell else do you want?

127
00:12:23,639 --> 00:12:24,559
Stop it!

128
00:12:24,739 --> 00:12:26,039
No more fighting, guys!

129
00:12:26,299 --> 00:12:29,359
Look, if we keep yelling, then the Marines are gonna go!

130
00:12:30,239 --> 00:12:31,699
Yeah, then shut up!

131
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:32,699
Say what?

132
00:12:32,899 --> 00:12:34,499
They should have gagged both of you!

133
00:12:34,559 --> 00:12:35,319
Yeah, whatever!

134
00:12:35,499 --> 00:12:36,859
Just a time of your...

135
00:12:36,859 --> 00:12:38,739
No fighting already!

136
00:12:38,739 --> 00:12:46,739
Uh, Captain T-Bone, what are you...

137
00:13:08,739 --> 00:13:13,639
Frankie's with them, too?

138
00:13:15,539 --> 00:13:16,319
Yes, sir.

139
00:13:16,499 --> 00:13:19,079
But I'm afraid that the C-Train has already departed.

140
00:13:19,459 --> 00:13:22,719
Pauly and the other guys are out looking for Straw Hat and his friends.

141
00:13:22,919 --> 00:13:23,739
But no luck.

142
00:13:26,619 --> 00:13:29,139
Now that we all know that Robin needs saving,

143
00:13:29,279 --> 00:13:31,459
then there's no limit to what we can accomplish.

144
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:36,879
Whoa!

145
00:13:36,879 --> 00:13:39,079
A secret base?

146
00:13:39,099 --> 00:13:42,379
It's been more than eight years since anyone set foot in here.

147
00:13:42,959 --> 00:13:46,439
And nobody's touched the C-Train for more than 12.

148
00:13:47,019 --> 00:13:48,059
Let's go, Chopper!

149
00:13:48,259 --> 00:13:48,599
Right!

150
00:13:48,999 --> 00:13:51,959
I'm warning you, the thing may not run anymore.

151
00:13:52,119 --> 00:13:52,719
What?

152
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:54,319
You better be kidding me!

153
00:13:58,159 --> 00:14:00,519
Now, now, settle down, boys.

154
00:14:00,919 --> 00:14:02,739
You can run as fast as you like,

155
00:14:02,819 --> 00:14:05,059
but you're not getting inside without the key.

156
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:06,159
Huh?

157
00:14:06,159 --> 00:14:07,739
Now that's weird.

158
00:14:08,379 --> 00:14:09,119
It's open!

159
00:14:13,319 --> 00:14:13,819
Whoa!

160
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:14,299
Awesome!

161
00:14:16,299 --> 00:14:17,299
Check out the face!

162
00:14:19,299 --> 00:14:20,299
So cool!

163
00:14:20,299 --> 00:14:25,919
Unlike the puffing tom, this one here's a crazy train.

164
00:14:26,379 --> 00:14:28,539
Its name is Rocket Man.

165
00:14:28,759 --> 00:14:32,359
Comes with no guarantees, so board at your own risk.

166
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:33,659
Rocket Man!

167
00:14:33,759 --> 00:14:34,439
Sounds fast!

168
00:14:35,439 --> 00:14:35,959
Neato!

169
00:14:35,959 --> 00:14:39,479
Did you have to add the face?

170
00:14:39,539 --> 00:14:42,639
Don't worry, it may be mean, but it won't bite.

171
00:14:45,519 --> 00:14:46,319
Hey, look!

172
00:14:46,379 --> 00:14:47,179
It's Ice Pops!

173
00:14:47,179 --> 00:14:49,219
Hello there, Straw Hat.

174
00:14:49,559 --> 00:14:51,339
So, you're okay after all.

175
00:14:51,739 --> 00:14:53,799
It seems your friend's faith was well-founded.

176
00:14:54,259 --> 00:14:55,939
I assume you brought them here, Kokoro?

177
00:14:56,219 --> 00:14:58,559
The question is, what are you doing here?

178
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:00,479
You've been through a lot today.

179
00:15:00,559 --> 00:15:01,539
You need rest.

180
00:15:01,799 --> 00:15:05,299
Well, let's just say you and I were thinking the same thing.

181
00:15:06,199 --> 00:15:08,799
We have a soft spot for idiots, don't we?

182
00:15:08,879 --> 00:15:10,879
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

183
00:15:10,879 --> 00:15:12,559
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

184
00:15:16,059 --> 00:15:16,919
Go ahead.

185
00:15:17,139 --> 00:15:18,639
I just finished servicing it.

186
00:15:18,859 --> 00:15:21,819
Water and coal have been loaded and the steam's building up now.

187
00:15:22,199 --> 00:15:22,879
Ha ha ha!

188
00:15:22,879 --> 00:15:25,039
Thanks for getting it ready for us!

189
00:15:25,079 --> 00:15:25,979
We owe you one!

190
00:15:26,219 --> 00:15:27,419
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

191
00:15:27,599 --> 00:15:28,059
Hmm.

192
00:15:28,319 --> 00:15:30,379
I wouldn't celebrate yet if I were you.

193
00:15:30,659 --> 00:15:32,599
You might not even survive the ride.

194
00:15:32,879 --> 00:15:35,639
This was our failed prototype before we made the Puffing Tom.

195
00:15:36,039 --> 00:15:38,559
No matter how you tune it, you can't control its speed.

196
00:15:39,399 --> 00:15:41,399
In other words, it's a runaway train.

197
00:15:42,819 --> 00:15:43,659
That's fine.

198
00:15:43,879 --> 00:15:45,879
It can go as fast as it wants.

199
00:15:46,879 --> 00:15:47,219
Hmph.

200
00:15:48,359 --> 00:15:49,199
Hurry up!

201
00:15:49,299 --> 00:15:50,019
Let's go!

202
00:15:50,719 --> 00:15:51,859
Get on already!

203
00:15:52,879 --> 00:15:55,719
We're leaving as soon as Nami gets here, Granny!

204
00:15:55,719 --> 00:15:59,719
Oh, man!

205
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:00,979
Luffy, are you okay?

206
00:16:01,319 --> 00:16:04,219
You've been kind of shaky on your feet since we found you.

207
00:16:04,379 --> 00:16:06,299
He probably just lost too much blood.

208
00:16:06,579 --> 00:16:07,479
Ugh, maybe.

209
00:16:07,819 --> 00:16:09,619
I am feeling kind of dizzy.

210
00:16:10,039 --> 00:16:11,659
I think I need some meat.

211
00:16:12,079 --> 00:16:13,099
Hurry, this way!

212
00:16:16,539 --> 00:16:17,099
Wait!

213
00:16:17,299 --> 00:16:20,559
I don't see why you have to go all the way down here just to eat your dinner!

214
00:16:20,719 --> 00:16:21,279
That's right!

215
00:16:21,279 --> 00:16:22,999
If you're hungry, eat now!

216
00:16:23,119 --> 00:16:24,619
You think all that food is for me?

217
00:16:24,819 --> 00:16:25,219
What?

218
00:16:25,899 --> 00:16:27,199
Sorry I took so long!

219
00:16:27,399 --> 00:16:27,719
Nami.

220
00:16:28,119 --> 00:16:28,539
Hey!

221
00:16:28,699 --> 00:16:30,099
Save the small talk for later!

222
00:16:30,399 --> 00:16:32,299
Get on board so we can go!

223
00:16:32,799 --> 00:16:33,819
Wow, amazing.

224
00:16:34,319 --> 00:16:35,939
So there's another sea train, huh?

225
00:16:36,939 --> 00:16:39,559
He was hiding here all this time and we never knew.

226
00:16:39,939 --> 00:16:41,019
This is a real surprise!

227
00:16:41,019 --> 00:16:43,119
You're the one who told us we have to hurry!

228
00:16:43,239 --> 00:16:44,879
Why are you the last one to get here?

229
00:16:45,099 --> 00:16:46,939
And what's with the big bag?

230
00:16:47,139 --> 00:16:48,319
I brought you food and drinks!

231
00:16:48,339 --> 00:16:50,039
I'm sorry I just yelled at you!

232
00:16:51,939 --> 00:16:53,279
He's ready to go!

233
00:16:53,739 --> 00:16:55,479
You'll shoot out of the canal into the ocean.

234
00:16:55,979 --> 00:16:58,879
If you can latch onto the railway after that, it should be a good start.

235
00:16:59,239 --> 00:17:00,599
Don't you worry a bit.

236
00:17:00,799 --> 00:17:03,059
I like to drink, but I take my job seriously.

237
00:17:03,659 --> 00:17:06,479
You just stay here and give that body of yours a good rest.

238
00:17:06,679 --> 00:17:07,739
Sounds fine to me.

239
00:17:07,939 --> 00:17:12,719
And while I'm taking care of these pirate folk, I hope you don't mind watching Gonby and Jimny for me.

240
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:14,179
Yes, that's fine.

241
00:17:14,179 --> 00:17:19,019
Don't go troubling yourself over him, either.

242
00:17:20,099 --> 00:17:22,619
That boy got hit by a sea train, you know.

243
00:17:22,939 --> 00:17:25,399
If he can survive that, I'm sure he'll be okay.

244
00:17:25,819 --> 00:17:28,559
Besides, we've got the king of the pirates on our side.

245
00:17:28,659 --> 00:17:29,699
We can't lose.

246
00:17:31,779 --> 00:17:32,039
Huh?

247
00:17:33,259 --> 00:17:33,659
Strawheads!

248
00:17:37,399 --> 00:17:38,419
Who's there?

249
00:17:39,619 --> 00:17:41,299
The Frankie family!

250
00:17:44,179 --> 00:17:47,239
We're kind of busy right now.

251
00:17:47,539 --> 00:17:48,959
Please, Straw Hat!

252
00:17:49,559 --> 00:17:50,839
You guys gotta take us!

253
00:21:55,180 --> 00:22:12,180
夢見た僕らは間違いじゃないと信じて 荒く埋める海原を渡って行ける

254
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:21,180
誰よりも浮かんで 思いやりもあるけれど

